import ../../../ui/scene_mesh_picking.dl
import ../../../ui/scene_surfaces.dl

to check transformed number {floating-point number:actual} equals {floating-point number:expected}:
    require condition ((the absolute value of (actual - expected)) < 0.00001) reporting "A shared scene transform or mesh pick changed."

to check transformed vector {vector:actual} equals {vector:expected}:
    check transformed number (the length of (actual - expected)) equals 0.0

set scale to a graphics scale by x 2.0 y 3.0 z 4.0
set rotation to a graphics rotation of 90.0 degrees around x 0.0 y 0.0 z 1.0
set translation to a graphics translation by x 10.0 y 2.0 z -3.0
set model to the graphics product of translation and (the graphics product of rotation and scale)
set transform to a UI scene transform from model
set x to a new vector with x 1.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0
set position to the UI scene position of x through transform
check transformed vector position equals (a new vector with x 10.0, y 4.0 and z -3.0)
check transformed vector (the UI scene position of position restored through transform) equals x
check transformed vector (the UI scene direction of x through transform) equals (a new vector with x 0.0, y 2.0 and z 0.0)
set normal to a new vector with x 1.0, y 1.0 and z 0.0
set expected to (a new vector with x (0.0 - 1.0 / 3.0), y 0.5 and z 0.0) normalized
check transformed vector (the UI scene normal of normal through transform) equals expected
set identity to the graphics product of (transform's matrix) and (transform's inverse)
set {identity matrix} to an identity graphics matrix
set index to 0
loop while index < 16:
    check transformed number (the item at index in identity) equals (the item at index in identity matrix)
    increment index
check transformed number (transform's handedness) equals 1.0
check transformed vector (the UI scene direction of (a new vector with x 1, y 0 and z 0) through transform) equals (a new vector with x 0.0, y 2.0 and z 0.0)

# Normals remain perpendicular to both surface tangents under shear.
set shear to an identity graphics matrix
store (0.5 as a 32 bit floating-point number) into shear at 4
set transform to a UI scene transform from shear
set tangent to a new vector with x 0.0, y 1.0 and z 0.0
set normal to the UI scene normal of x through transform
check transformed number (the dot product of normal and (the UI scene direction of tangent through transform)) equals 0.0
check transformed number (the length of normal) equals 1.0
set transform to a UI scene transform from (a graphics scale by x -2.0 y 3.0 z 4.0)
check transformed vector (the UI scene normal of x through transform) equals (a new vector with x -1.0, y 0.0 and z 0.0)
check transformed number (transform's handedness) equals -1.0

set box to a UI box mesh with 1 by 1 by 1 segments
check transformed number (box's bounds' minimum's x) equals -0.5
check transformed number (box's bounds' maximum's z) equals 0.5
set model to the graphics product of (a graphics translation by x 1.0 y 2.0 z 3.0) and (a graphics scale by x 2.0 y 4.0 z 6.0)
set transform to a UI scene transform from model
set ray to a new UI scene ray
set ray's origin to a new vector with x 1.0, y 2.0 and z 20.0
set ray's direction to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z -2.0
set hit to the UI scene hit from ray on mesh box through transform including backfaces false
require condition (hit's hit) reporting "A ray missed a transformed box."
check transformed vector (hit's point) equals (a new vector with x 1.0, y 2.0 and z 6.0)
check transformed number (hit's distance) equals 14.0
set ray's origin to a new vector with x 2.0, y 2.0 and z 20.0
require condition ((the UI scene hit from ray on mesh box through transform including backfaces false)'s hit) reporting "A ray on a box boundary was incorrectly culled."
set ray's origin to a new vector with x 10.0, y 2.0 and z 20.0
require condition (((the UI scene hit from ray on mesh box through transform including backfaces false)'s hit) = false) reporting "A parallel ray outside the mesh bounds reported a hit."
set ray's origin to a new vector with x 1.0, y 2.0 and z 20.0
set ray's direction to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 1.0
require condition (((the UI scene hit from ray on mesh box through transform including backfaces true)'s hit) = false) reporting "A mesh behind the ray reported a hit."
set ray's origin to a new vector with x 1.0, y 2.0 and z 3.0
require condition (((the UI scene hit from ray on mesh box through transform including backfaces false)'s hit) = false) reporting "An inside ray selected a backface of a closed mesh."
set hit to the UI scene hit from ray on mesh box through transform including backfaces true
require condition (hit's hit) reporting "An inside ray missed a two-sided mesh."
check transformed number (hit's distance) equals 3.0

set rotation to a graphics rotation of 45.0 degrees around x 0.0 y 1.0 z 0.0
set model to the graphics product of rotation and (a graphics scale by x 2.0 y 4.0 z 6.0)
set transform to a UI scene transform from model
set ray's origin to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 10.0
set ray's direction to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z -1.0
set hit to the UI scene hit from ray on mesh box through transform including backfaces false
require condition (hit's hit) reporting "A ray missed a rotated and unevenly scaled mesh."
check transformed number (hit's point's z) equals (the square root of 2.0)
check transformed number (hit's distance) equals (10.0 - the square root of 2.0)

# Mirroring preserves the mesh's outward-facing side, as in scene rendering.
set transform to a UI scene transform from (a graphics scale by x -2.0 y 3.0 z 4.0)
set ray's origin to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z 10.0
set ray's direction to a new vector with x 0.0, y 0.0 and z -1.0
set hit to the UI scene hit from ray on mesh box through transform including backfaces false
require condition (hit's hit) reporting "Mirroring inverted a mesh's outward-facing side."
check transformed number (hit's distance) equals 8.0
set empty to a new UI scene mesh
require condition (((the UI scene hit from ray on mesh empty through transform including backfaces true)'s hit) = false) reporting "An empty scene mesh reported a hit."
print line "Scene transforms share affine inverses, inverse-transpose normals, mirrored handedness, bounds and nearest world-distance mesh picking."
